{"id":569,"flavor":[{"games":["Shield"],"text":"The toxic liquid it launches from its right arm is so virulent that it can kill a weakened creature instantly."},{"games":["Sword"],"text":"This Pokémon eats trash, which turns into poison inside its body. The main component of the poison depends on what sort of trash was eaten."},{"games":["Ultra Moon"],"text":"Some say the reason Garbodor in Alola are a little stronger than their counterparts elsewhere is the presence of Muk, their natural enemy."},{"games":["Ultra Sun"],"text":"It locks opponents in place with its left hand, immobilizing them by entirely dousing their bodies with poisonous liquid."},{"games":["Moon"],"text":"For a time, their numbers increased explosively in Alola. Since the arrival of Grimer, their population has decreased dramatically."},{"games":["Sun"],"text":"Beware the poisonous liquid it shoots from its right arm. If even a little of it gets on you, you’ll experience the effects of the unidentified toxin."},{"games":["Alpha Sapphire","Y","White 2","Black 2"],"text":"Consuming garbage makes new kinds of poison gases and liquids inside their bodies."},{"games":["Omega Ruby","X","Black"],"text":"It clenches opponents with its left arm and finishes them off with foul-smelling poison gas belched from its mouth."},{"games":["White"],"text":"They absorb garbage and make it part of their bodies. They shoot a poisonous liquid from their right-hand fingertips."}],"abilities":[{"name":"Stench","hidden":false,"description":"By releasing a stench when attacking, the Pokémon may cause the target to flinch."},{"name":"Weak Armor","hidden":false,"description":"The Pokémon's Defense stat is lowered when it takes damage from physical moves, but its Speed stat is sharply boosted."},{"name":"Aftermath","hidden":true,"description":"Damages the attacker if it knocks out the Pokémon with a move that makes direct contact."}],"eggGroups":["Mineral"],"genderRate":4,"hatchCounter":20,"baseHappiness":70,"growthRate":"me